+### Stage 3, started and paused (agent timetables, tree tw/timetables from 57d37920, 2026-11-22)
+
+Paused by the orchestrator (Anita keeping tokens for bug fixes). Nothing landed. **The tree does not compile yet**:
+about 45 errors in wasm/lines.rs and world.rs, all from the widened place arrays (`[_; 5]` to `[_; PLACES]`,
+`Extra`'s `[_; 2]` to `[_; 3]`). Pick up by running `agent_cargo.py cargo check --profile agent --message-format short`
+and fixing each site; the sites are listed below.
+
+**Decided (advisor agreed, 2026-11-22)**
+- Detailed starts from the line's rows as they are (Simple's three: 6-20, 20-24, 0-6; at four periods rush becomes
+  two rows with the same values), and a one-click preset gives demand's five periods (6-10, 10-16, 16-20, 20-24,
+  0-6). DECISIONS draft: "2026-11-22 (agent timetables, T-3346 stage 3): Detailed starts from the line's current
+  rows (moving up a mode keeps everything) and offers demand's five periods as one click; a Detailed row is at
+  least 2 hours (her T-3542 call), whole hours, up to 6 a day."
+- Detailed is the per-line idea: Simple follows the game's periods and hours (the game-wide Periods 3/4/5 control
+  stays), Detailed is the line's own rows. It replaces T-3542's "Set for this line" / "This line" / "Same as game"
+  (her 11-19 placement, so list those strings as removed and mark it her call). Lines saved with their own 3/4/5
+  periods show as Detailed; any Detailed layout edit turns them into plain rows.
+- Run on: Weekends (a weekend-only line) is stage 4: weekend riders are the weekday solve scaled, so the line
+  would get no riders without a demand change, which is hers. Run on: Weekdays is cheap if zero weekend counts
+  already work (verify); stage 3 may offer Every day / Weekdays only.
+- Name in DECISIONS or fix: the mixed-slot lies from T-3542 (hand weekend counts not read in a mixed slot, mixed
+  slots not paced at merges, a borrowed hour checked against averaged capacity) become the normal case for
+  Detailed lines.
+
+**The model, as written so far**
+- `params.rs`: `PLACES = 6` (0-2 the three rows' arrays, 3-5 `Extra`'s; place 5 is a Detailed line's sixth row);
+  `places`/`unplace` take and give `[T; 3]` extras. `Layout { n, start: [u8; 6], place: [u8; 6] }`: a line's day
+  as stretches with the place each runs. `Layout::of_rows(cuts, n)` is a 3/4/5-row line's (five stretches,
+  `PERIOD_PLACE`'s places), so Simple lines take exactly the old path. `Layout::free(starts)` builds Detailed rows:
+  rotated so the row in force at 6:00 is first, places `FREE_PLACES = [0, 3, 4, 1, 2, 5]`, so the five-period
+  preset equals "this line at 5 rows, default hours" (Mix None: the to-the-bit proof). `Layout::ok` (1-6
+  stretches, 2 h each, distinct places), `layout_pieces` (was `day_pieces`, which now wraps it),
+  `layout_shortest_h` (was `shortest_row_h`, which wraps it).
+- `net.rs`: `Extra` arrays widened to 3; `Extra::layout` (n 0 = not Detailed); `of_high` leaves place 5 empty so
+  Simple saves round-trip; `Mix::of(&Layout, n, period_slot)`, `Mix::w` per `PLACES`.
+- `net/service.rs`: `rows(l)` is 5 for a Detailed line (all five slots worked); new `free(l)`, `layout(l)`,
+  `row_places(l)` (replaces `ROW_PLACES[rows - 3]`); `extra_of(l, s)` gives three (the sixth from the slot its
+  row runs alone in); `row_slots`, `same_places` and the `0..5` place loops use `PLACES` / `row_places`.
+- `save.rs` (edited, not yet compiled): new trailing block `LDL1` **before** `LPD1` (its slots depend on Detailed
+  lines): count, per line index, n, starts, places, then place 5's trains, headway, weekend count, weekend
+  headway; written only where some line is Detailed, so Simple saves stay byte for byte. LPD1 still writes places
+  3-4 only (8 values). Still to do: bump `LEVEL` (38 now) and add `b"LDL1"` to `BLOCKS`; the shonei-server
+  walk step (count u; per line index u, n u, n starts, n places, 4 u); check `encode_eras` ERA4 takes place 5 and up
+  to 11 pieces (`PIECES_MAX` 12 holds).
+
+**Left in the sim**
+- Fix the compile errors: wasm/lines.rs (209-211 clearing `x`, `train_counts`/weekend setters' `[c[0]; 2]` to
+  three, `set_line_row_*` and `line_row_*`, `line_rows`, `line_row_weekend`: use `row_places(l)` and `PLACES`),
+  world.rs (`rows_ops` remap 417-447, and lines near 550, 960-1021, 1136-1140, 1807, 1827, 1984, 2124-2132:
+  arrays of places), wasm.rs 266 (`ROW_PLACES`), boarding.rs 568 (hash the layout, not `hours(l)`), and the timing
+  retime key (must include the layout).
+- Check per the advisor: `running_borrowed`, `auto_counts`, `trim_auto`, `places_most` with a row that is the main
+  place in no slot (say 12-14 inside midday).
+- Ops: `set_line_layout(id, starts, from)` where `from[i]` is the current row (in `line_row_trains` order) each new
+  row copies its values from (trains, headway, weekend counts and headways); one undoable batch on the `rows_ops`
+  pattern (`Op::Rows { line, 0 }`, `Op::Hours { line, [0; 5] }`, `Op::Extra` with the layout and values,
+  counts/auto/weekend ops). Split = same `from` twice; remove = the neighbour keeps its values; preset = `from` by
+  most overlap. Empty starts = back to Simple, each game row taking the most of the Detailed rows it overlaps.
+- Proofs: the preset equals "This line 5" to the bit; a Rust test on "6-9 12, 9-16 6, 16-19 12, 19-24 4, 0-6 2"
+  (departures, round trips per row, demand headways by hand).
+
+**Left in the app** (not started): mode Simple / Detailed in the panel heading; Detailed rows (hours box, steppers,
+split and remove icons, "6 rows at most", preset button); the question going back to Simple; one `lineRows(st)`
+behind every `rowsOf(n)[r]` (schedule.tsx, SchedulePanel, lineRunning, LineInspector 681, newLine); capLoad, Set
+as default and the `high_rows` setters skip Detailed lines; grep checks/ for the per-line period controls.
